WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.556 --> 00:00:16.799
July, Pollyanna often told Aunt Polly how happy she was.

2
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.144
Aunt Polly usually replied, "It's nice that your days are happy, but that's not enough.

3
00:00:24.265 --> 00:00:28.188
They must also be profitable, or I've failed in my duty to you."

4
00:00:30.608 --> 00:00:34.391
Pollyanna answered with hugs and kisses, which Aunt Polly found alarming.

5
00:00:36.812 --> 00:00:40.014
But one day during a sewing lesson, Pollyanna asked.

6
00:00:40.034 --> 00:00:43.737
"What does having a 'profitable' day mean?"

7
00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:49.961
"Why, it means having something to show for the day," Aunt Polly said.

8
00:00:49.981 --> 00:00:54.644
"So, just being glad isn't profitable?"

9
00:00:54.664 --> 00:00:57.346
"Certainly not."

10
00:00:58.627 --> 00:01:00.448
Aunt Polly rapped her thimble on the table.

11
00:01:01.708 --> 00:01:05.431
"Oh! Then I'm afraid you'll never want to play the game."

12
00:01:05.451 --> 00:01:09.215
"Game? What game?"

13
00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:13.818
"The game that Fath—" Pollyanna clapped her hand over her mouth.

14
00:01:13.838 --> 00:01:16.841
"I mean, it's nothing."

15
00:01:16.861 --> 00:01:23.327
"That's enough for this morning," Aunt Polly said, and their sewing lesson was over.

16
00:01:25.128 --> 00:01:29.292
That afternoon Pollyanna was going down the attic stairs when she met Aunt Polly coming up.

17
00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.241
"You're coming to see me!"

18
00:01:32.622 --> 00:01:34.143
Pollyanna cried with delight.

19
00:01:35.484 --> 00:01:38.587
She scampered back up the stairs and threw open her door in welcome.

20
00:01:39.988 --> 00:01:42.070
Aunt Polly had not intended to visit her niece.

21
00:01:43.331 --> 00:01:46.274
Instead she'd planned to look for a shawl in the main part of the attic.

22
00:01:48.216 --> 00:01:51.899
So she was surprised to find herself sitting in a chair in Pollyanna's room.

23
00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.884
Then again, she'd often found herself doing surprising things since Pollyanna's arrival.

24
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.001
"I love having visitors!"

25
00:02:00.402 --> 00:02:01.202
Pollyanna said.

26
00:02:01.222 --> 00:02:08.287
"And I love this room, even though it doesn't have the carpets and curtains and pictures I—" She

27
00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:08.947
stopped short.

28
00:02:10.468 --> 00:02:11.389
Her aunt looked at her.

29
00:02:11.409 --> 00:02:13.750
"What's that, Pollyanna?"

30
00:02:15.672 --> 00:02:17.673
Pollyanna turned red with embarrassment.

31
00:02:18.994 --> 00:02:20.855
"I didn't mean to say that."

32
00:02:20.875 --> 00:02:24.298
"Maybe not."

33
00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.460
There was a note of coldness in Aunt Polly's voice.

34
00:02:28.896 --> 00:02:31.698
"But you did say it, so let's hear the rest."

35
00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:40.763
"It was nothing really, just that I'd been planning on pretty carpets and lace curtains and—" "Planning on

36
00:02:40.843 --> 00:02:43.364
them?" Aunt Polly interrupted sharply.

37
00:02:44.665 --> 00:02:47.927
Pollyanna turned even redder as she tried to apologize.

38
00:02:47.947 --> 00:02:52.029
"It was only because I'd never had pretty things.

39
00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:56.232
I mean, we had two rugs from the donation box.

40
00:02:57.288 --> 00:02:59.870
But one had ink spots and the other had holes.

41
00:03:01.591 --> 00:03:04.913
And Fath—I mean, we had two nice pictures.

42
00:03:06.074 --> 00:03:10.597
We sold one though to buy me shoes, and the glass broke on another one."

43
00:03:12.639 --> 00:03:15.701
Aunt Polly listened without interrupting as Pollyanna went on.

44
00:03:15.721 --> 00:03:22.025
"When I walked through your house that first day, I shouldn't have been planning how pretty my room

45
00:03:22.046 --> 00:03:22.446
would be.

46
00:03:23.807 --> 00:03:28.926
But truly, Aunt Polly, in only a few minutes I was glad that this was my room.

47
00:03:28.946 --> 00:03:34.608
I was so glad that the bureau didn't have a mirror because I didn't want to see my

48
00:03:34.668 --> 00:03:40.431
freckles! There couldn't be a nicer picture than the view from my window.

49
00:03:41.731 --> 00:03:43.472
And you've been so good to me."

50
00:03:45.093 --> 00:03:46.933
Now it was Aunt Polly's turn to blush.

51
00:03:48.254 --> 00:03:52.376
She suddenly rose to her feet and said stiffly, "You've said quite enough."

52
00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.545
The next minute Aunt Polly swept downstairs, leaving a baffled Pollyanna behind.

53
00:04:00.986 --> 00:04:05.190
It was only when Aunt Polly reached the first floor that she realized she'd forgotten the shawl.

54
00:04:08.413 --> 00:04:10.315
In the morning Aunt Polly spoke to Nancy.

55
00:04:10.335 --> 00:04:14.259
"Today you may move Miss Pollyanna's things to the room below."

56
00:04:14.279 --> 00:04:18.804
"Yes, ma'am," Nancy said quietly.

57
00:04:21.424 --> 00:04:25.105
A few minutes later, Nancy broke the happy news to Pollyanna in the attic.

58
00:04:27.526 --> 00:04:29.466
Nancy gathered up an armload of clothes.

59
00:04:29.486 --> 00:04:33.427
"I'll hurry and take your things down before Miss Polly changes her mind."

60
00:04:35.068 --> 00:04:38.749
Pollyanna went flying downstairs, taking the steps two at a time.

61
00:04:40.569 --> 00:04:44.590
She banged two doors and knocked over a chair before finding her aunt in the sitting room.

62
00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.451
"Oh, Aunt Polly, thank you!

63
00:04:47.831 --> 00:04:50.732
That room has everything I ever wanted!"

64
00:04:54.056 --> 00:04:59.601
"I'm glad you like it, and I trust you'll take proper care of everything," Aunt Polly said.

65
00:04:59.621 --> 00:05:04.344
"But please pick up that chair, and stop banging doors."

66
00:05:05.625 --> 00:05:09.669
She would have said more, but for some strange reason, she felt like crying.

67
00:05:09.689 --> 00:05:14.933
"I'm sorry I banged the doors, but I was just so happy!

68
00:05:15.894 --> 00:05:18.055
Did you ever bang doors when you were happy?"

69
00:05:18.075 --> 00:05:20.678
"Certainly not!"

70
00:05:21.718 --> 00:05:23.380
Aunt Polly was shocked at the thought.

71
00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:28.786
"Oh, that's a shame because that means you were never glad about something."

72
00:05:30.048 --> 00:05:35.135
Before Aunt Polly could reply, Pollyanna dashed back upstairs to help Nancy move her things.
